TITLE: Augmenting Zero-Shot Performance with Web-based Auxiliary Knowledge
PROPOSAL: We develop an auxiliary knowledge retrieval system that gathers contextual background information about procedural steps (e.g. tool usage, ingredient preparation) from web descriptions and unstructured text sources. The retrieved knowledge is utilized to augment the multimodal graph feature space, providing a denser and more informative representation that better captures task-specific concepts. During evaluation, we heuristically search for web information relevant to the procedural steps being evaluated, using this pre-processed knowledge to fine-tune step similarity scores.
